   }
   ```

3. **Underlying Formatter**: The underlying type is formatted using `underlying_formatter`, which maps to the underlying type's formatter (lines 97–101):
   ```cpp
   template <typename E, typename Char>
   using underlying_formatter = formatter<mapped_t<underlying_t<E>, Char>, Char>;
   ```

   For example, when formatting an enum annotated with `fmt::as_underlying`, it delegates to the base `underlying_formatter` via `format_as(value)` (lines 257–268):
   ```cpp
   template <typename FormatContext>
   auto format(E value, FormatContext& ctx) const -> decltype(ctx.out()) {
     using base = detail::underlying_formatter<E, Char>;
     return base::format(format_as(value), ctx);
   }
   ```
